This is the easiest way for me to identify scrolls also.  If you have 18
charisma (or thereabouts), they're 14 zorkmids give or take
(blessed/cursed status can make a difference).  The next cheapest is
light, I believe, and it's not even close.

However, that said, I don't wait around to identify scrolls.  I'm an
impatient sort of nethacker...I want to plow throw things with a minimum
fuss.  That's why I like playing classes like Barbarians (and now
Cavemen, since I like a challenge).  "Ug.  Me drink potion.  Me read
scroll."  If I have important armor, I'll take it off before reading an
unidentified scroll.  Likewise, I'll drop my potions, scrolls and
spellbooks and make sure I'm at full hit points (or in the neighborhood)
in case it is a scroll of fire (I also make sure that I'm not standing
near anything friendly).  So, really, the only scrolls that hurt me are
amnesia (spells, shmells, who needs 'em?) and punishment (which are rare
enough that I've gone through entire ascentions without finding one). 
So, I play the odds.  Sometimes I get burned (see:  cursed scrolls of
create monster) but that's the way the wishing wand crumbles.

As for potions, I'm a sucker.  I just quaff the damn things.  "Sickness?
 Bah.  Blindness?  Me have telepathy.  Paralysis?  Bah.  Confusion? 
Doesn't last very long.  Me quaff."

